From 5ea716b91d00ac38994d502c6ef58e8792479d1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian MDG <christian@heigraduate.local>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 07:31:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(exam): add mandatory SEMESTRE FK on EXAM (MCD fix #11)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EXAM was only linked to COURS + ANNEE_UNIVERSITAIRE, never to SEMESTRE,
even though the corrected MCD (correction #11) requires it: since
course_track (V42_25) now lets the same course sit at different
semesters depending on the parcours, an exam without a semester_id
is ambiguous about which semester it actually belongs to.

- New migration V42_28: adds exam.semester_id as a nullable column
  first, backfills it in two passes (exact date-range match against
  the exam's own `date` column, then a same-academic-year fallback
  for any exam dated outside every semester, mirroring the fallback
  used in V42_25), then makes it NOT NULL. Existing rows are never
  left orphaned by this migration.
- Exam entity: added a mandatory `semester` (@ManyToOne(optional =
  false), JoinColumn nullable = false), consistent with the MCD
  cardinality "SEMESTRE ||--o{ EXAMEN" (mandatory), as opposed to
  the optional FK already used on AFFECTATION.
- ExamRequest/ExamResponse/ExamMapper: added semesterId (+
  semesterLabel on the response), same field-naming convention as
  AssignmentRequest/AssignmentResponse.
- ExamService: added SemesterRepository and a `resolveSemester`
  helper (same pattern as AssignmentService.resolveOptionalSemester,
  but mandatory instead of optional) that 404s on an unknown
  semesterId and 400s if the semester does not belong to the
  request's academicYearId, used in both create() and update().
- ExamServiceTest: updated all existing cases to supply a semester,
  and added three new cases: semester not found, semester belonging
  to a different academic year, and asserting the new response
  fields are populated correctly.

Grep audit: no other file references Exam.getSemester() or
constructs ExamRequest/ExamResponse positionally outside the files
touched above (GradeService/GradeMapper only ever read
exam.getId()/getLabel()/getCourse()/getCoefficient(), never
semester), so this change is isolated to the EXAM module.

Note for whoever runs this migration: pass 2 of the backfill only
covers the case where an academic year has at least one semester.
If any academic year referenced by an existing exam has zero
semester rows, V42_28 will fail on the final NOT NULL constraint —
same pre-existing risk as V42_24/V42_25, flagged here for visibility.
